A||N||5||WhiteFieroBlur||How do you screw in the other mirror screw?||||5||
Z||000000||WhiteFieroBlur||11-16-2001||12:40 PM||||I have had both problems with both my mirrors coming off and had to replace one and screw the other back in. I only have the one screw in thats easy to get to but I am worried thats its not enough. Is there some kinda trick to get to the other screw? I don't know how to take off the dew strip so I dunno what to do. ||||reg||5
Z||000001||JohnF||11-16-2001||12:46 PM||||Hmmmmm?  I just removed and replaced my driver's side mirror.  Inner door panel must be removed then forward end cap (3 screws) must be removed.  You should, then, have access to the 2 nuts retaining the miirror.  <P>BTW - you are more than half-way to replacing the dew wipe at that point.  Just go-ahead and do it!||||reg||14
Z||000002||WhiteFieroBlur||11-16-2001||01:41 PM||||Don't you have to have some kind of tool to get that dew strip off? I just never tried to mess with it just yet. Also I have done all that, but no tool wrench that I have will just fit over there and allow me to screw it in without maybe accidently dropping a collection of nuts down in the door.||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnF||11-16-2001||02:00 PM||||It's better (but not absolutely necessary) to have a tool the is sold by Rodney Dickman - see it on his web site - about $10.00, I think.<P>Do a little reading about the replacement.  It's straightforward after you remove the inner door panel - you DO NOT need to remove the outer skin.<P>After you replace the dew strip, you'll love yourself forever.||||reg||6
Z||000004||cadaver||11-16-2001||09:05 PM||||The special tool I use for the mirrors is a 10mm box wrench.||||reg||1
Z||000005||cadaver||11-16-2001||09:07 PM||||Oh and they are nuts and studs. Are yours missing and replaced with screws?||||reg||1
